{"duration_api_ms":6011,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"453fa6f3-28e7-40e5-b535-04eefb01cea9","total_cost_usd":0.00109,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1057,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1417,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1063},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1057,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1057},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1601,"outputTokens":1437,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1057,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00109,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1063,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1057,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Thresholds:** The $0.01-per-share and 0.5%-of-NAV figures are materiality triggers set by fund boards, not statutory limits. Many funds apply them as \"whichever is greater,\" though wording varies by fund. Errors breaching the threshold generally require correction and may require shareholder compensation. Smaller errors are typically logged and monitored but not remediated.\n\n**Governance:** Correction is governed by board-approved valuation and pricing-error policies, operating under Rule 38a-1 (compliance programs) and Rule 2a-5 (fair value determinations and board oversight). The administrator executes corrections and reports to the board, usually via the valuation or pricing committee. Those policies set compensation methodology and the treatment of affected creations and redemptions. Rule 22c-1 governs redemption and purchase pricing.\n\n**Practical notes:** NAV errors affect authorized participants as well as shareholders, so the administrator should confirm treatment of affected transactions. Verify thresholds and procedures against the fund's policy documents and counsel's guidance.","ttft_ms":4595,"type":"result","duration_ms":5556,"uuid":"6aa23f46-dd19-4060-8e63-316607d26d1e","ttft_stream_ms":832,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":832,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
